Z||000003||Fierowrecker||07-14-2001||07:59 PM||||Hey Grinthock!<BR>Does the door close firmly, or is it still loose?<BR>If it is loose, then the mechanizm that holds the pin could be out of adjustment...<BR>If it feels firm, then you may need to remove the door panel to see if it has something loose inside...<BR>Course, it may need the hinge pins replaced...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrgone||07-14-2001||08:28 PM||||on the little knobs that stick out of the car (not the door) that the door latches on to doesnt have a rubber cap on it it will rattle just like my car.||||reg||1
Z||000005||grinthock||07-15-2001||12:41 AM||||Thanks guys I will check it all tommorow I have a feeling that the mech who was working on it leaned hard on it||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||07-15-2001||03:44 PM||||Sloppy hinge pins will also make it rattle. before and adjustment to the hinges or strick those must be fixed.<P>If it's inside the door it could be any number of things. bent rods, rubber bumpers missing, something fell inside the door...||||reg||1
